<figure class="bsn-walkthrough" aria-labelledby="bsn-walkthrough-title">
  <div class="walkthrough-heading">
    <h4 id="bsn-walkthrough-title">Chat/2 LeaveRequest</h4>
    <p><code>42 35</code> is a verified client-to-server <code>Chat/2 LeaveRequest</code>
    for channel index 6.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="record-bytes" aria-label="The two bytes 42 and 35 split into command, service flag, service slot, channel index, and padding">
    <div class="record-byte">
      <div class="record-byte-label"><b>byte 0</b><code>0x42</code></div>
      <div class="record-bit-labels" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>7</span><span>6</span><span>5</span><span>4</span><span>3</span><span>2</span><span>1</span><span>0</span>
      </div>
      <div class="record-bit-fields">
        <span class="record-slot-head"><b>0</b><small>slot</small></span>
        <span class="record-service"><b>1</b><small>service</small></span>
        <span class="record-command"><b>000010</b><small>command 2</small></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="record-byte">
      <div class="record-byte-label"><b>byte 1</b><code>0x35</code></div>
      <div class="record-bit-labels" aria-hidden="true">
        <span>7</span><span>6</span><span>5</span><span>4</span><span>3</span><span>2</span><span>1</span><span>0</span>
      </div>
      <div class="record-bit-fields">
        <span class="record-padding"><b>00</b><small>pad</small></span>
        <span class="record-payload"><b>110</b><small>channel 6</small></span>
        <span class="record-slot-tail"><b>101</b><small>slot 5</small></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table class="walkthrough-table">
    <caption>The byte diagrams use ordinary hex-display order, bit 7 through bit 0. The decoder consumes each byte from bit 0 through bit 7.</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Cursor range</th><th>Read</th><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>byte 0, bits 0..5</code></td><td>6 bits</td><td><code>2</code></td><td>Command 2</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>byte 0, bit 6</code></td><td>1 bit</td><td><code>1</code></td><td>A service slot follows</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>byte 0, bit 7</code><br><code>byte 1, bits 0..2</code></td><td>1 + 3 bits</td><td><code>0 || 101₂ = 5</code></td><td>Service slot 5, <code>Chat</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>byte 1, bits 3..5</code></td><td>3 bits</td><td><code>110₂ = 6</code></td><td><code>LeaveRequest.channelIndex</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>byte 1, bits 6..7</code></td><td>2 bits</td><td><code>00₂</code></td><td>Zero padding through the byte boundary</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="walkthrough-result">
    <p><b>Route lookup</b><br><code>(client → server, slot 5, command 2)</code> → <code>Chat::LeaveRequest</code></p>
    <p><b>Selected payload schema</b><br><code>channelIndex: u3</code></p>
    <p><b>Record boundary</b><br><code>11 route + 3 payload + 2 pad = 16 bits = 2 bytes</code></p>
  </div>

  <figcaption>Every Sunken service record follows this sequence: read the route,
  select its payload schema, decode that payload with the same bit cursor, then
  consume zero padding through the next byte boundary.</figcaption>
</figure>
